Author: Muath Zahir <muathzaher2004@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 27 17:36:40 2026 +0000

    ticket(1): shared <Markdown> component, wired into every prose surface

    Nothing in apps/web rendered markdown — DocPeek printed a <pre> of the file,
    the map's prose sections were raw text in a div, and ticket goal/context were
    plain divs full of unrendered backticks. One component now renders all of them.

    Built on react-markdown + remark-gfm (agents write GFM). Raw HTML passthrough
    stays off — no rehype plugin for it, so HTML in a doc is escaped rather than
    mounted — and there is no highlighter; a styled <pre><code> in JetBrains Mono
    is enough for prose docs with occasional snippets.

    MARKDOWN_POLICY is exported as plain data and pinned by test: with no DOM
    environment in this repo the component's output can't be asserted, and its
    behaviour is upstream's, so the policy is the only honest seam. Visual
    correctness was checked against the feature's committed prototype.html, which
    the `.md` rules are copied from.

    The `.md` block sets its own font-family and white-space so it renders the same
    inside .map-section-body and .td-body, which are mono/pre-wrap containers — that
    avoids restructuring either call site, which later tickets rebuild.

